        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Block, Alan Freed, Dick Clark, Delilah Rene, Ameen Sayani, Wolfman Jack, Casey Kasem, Don Imus, Howard Stern, Mike Francesa, Rush Limbaugh, Skip Kelly, Ryan Seacrest, Danny Bonaduce, Matt Siegel, Dale Dorman\n- Roles: Radio personalities, pop music radio hosts, shock jocks, sports talk hosts, political talk hosts, author, songwriter\n- Places: North Bend, Oregon, United States\n- Programs: Nationally syndicated nightly radio song request and dedication program\n\nFacts:\n- Delilah Rene was born on February 15, 1960, in North Bend, Oregon.\n- Delilah Rene is an American radio personality, author, and songwriter.\n- Delilah Rene is best known as the host of a nationally syndicated nightly U.S. radio song request and dedication program with an estimated 8 million listeners.\n- Notable radio personalities include pop music radio hosts Martin Block, Alan Freed, Dick Clark, Delilah Rene, Ameen Sayani, Wolfman Jack, and Casey Kasem.\n- Notable radio personalities also include shock jocks Don Imus and Howard Stern, sports talk host Mike Francesa, and political talk host Rush Limbaugh.\n- On air, Skip Kelly has shared the same mic as Ryan Seacrest, Danny Bonaduce, Delilah Rene, Matt Siegel, and Dale Dorman.",
